From: OpenWrt CI maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allow opt-in AX5 JDCloud HS400 experiments

Historical profile, blocked by prepare after runtime I/O failures.
Kept for provenance and reproduction tests.

Apply only after the conservative eMMC patch and only for the explicitly
selected hs400 build profile. Advertise an 8-bit bus and HS400 at the
existing 192 MHz maximum clock. Do not enable enhanced strobe or alter
voltage supplies, CPU OPPs, partitions or reserved memory.

The eMMC advertises HS400 support, but PCB wiring is not verified.
Initialization fallback is best effort; use external backup and an
independent recovery path. This is not the default/release profile.

--- a/target/linux/qualcommax/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq6000-ax5-jdcloud.dts
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommax/files/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq6000-ax5-jdcloud.dts
@@ -17,3 +17,3 @@
 	status = "okay";
-	bus-width = <4>;
+	bus-width = <8>;
 	non-removable;
@@ -22,5 +22,5 @@
 
-	/delete-property/ mmc-hs400-1_8v;
+	mmc-hs400-1_8v;
 	mmc-hs200-1_8v;
 	mmc-ddr-1_8v;
 };
